    'intro'  => '<p>Cleveland&rsquo;s mid-term rental market is shaped heavily by healthcare. The Cleveland Clinic and University Hospitals are among the biggest employers in the region, and their campuses draw travel nurses, visiting physicians, residents, researchers and patients&rsquo; families who need furnished housing for weeks or months.</p><p><strong>University Circle</strong>, on the east side, is the city&rsquo;s cultural and medical center, home to Case Western Reserve University, University Hospitals and major museums, with Little Italy and Cleveland Heights close by. On the west side, <strong>Ohio City</strong> and <strong>Tremont</strong> offer restored homes, breweries and restaurants near downtown, and Lakewood is a dense inner suburb with plenty of apartments.</p><p>Winters bring cold and lake-effect snow, so ask about heating, parking and snow removal when you book a stay between November and March. Many medical renters prefer the east side for the short trip to the Clinic and UH, while people working downtown often choose the west side.</p>',
    'neighborhoods' => [
      ['name' => 'University Circle', 'blurb' => 'Home to Case Western Reserve, University Hospitals and major museums. The most convenient area for medical and university stays.'],
      ['name' => 'Little Italy', 'blurb' => 'A compact historic neighborhood next to University Circle with restaurants and older apartments.'],
      ['name' => 'Ohio City', 'blurb' => 'A west-side neighborhood around the West Side Market with breweries and restaurants, a quick ride to downtown.'],
      ['name' => 'Tremont', 'blurb' => 'A hilltop neighborhood south of Ohio City known for dining and views of downtown.'],
      ['name' => 'Detroit-Shoreway and Gordon Square', 'blurb' => 'A west-side arts district near the lake with theaters and newer development.'],
      ['name' => 'Cleveland Heights', 'blurb' => 'An inner-ring suburb with the Coventry and Cedar-Lee districts, popular with grad students and medical staff.'],
      ['name' => 'Lakewood', 'blurb' => 'A walkable west-side suburb with many apartments along Detroit and Madison avenues.'],
    ],
    'prices' => '<p>Cleveland is one of the more affordable large metros in the country. Furnished private rooms commonly advertise in roughly the $500&ndash;$900 per month range, and entire furnished one-bedrooms typically run higher, often $1,000&ndash;$1,800 depending on neighborhood and building.</p><p>Newer buildings in University Circle, downtown and Ohio City tend to cost more. Treat these as ballpark numbers that shift with season, neighborhood and furnishing, and check current listings before deciding.</p>',
    'transit'=> '<p>The Greater Cleveland Regional Transit Authority (RTA) runs the Red Line rapid transit train from Cleveland Hopkins International Airport through downtown to University Circle and beyond, plus the HealthLine bus rapid transit along Euclid Avenue connecting downtown with the Cleveland Clinic and University Circle. The Blue and Green lines serve Shaker Heights.</p><p>Cleveland Hopkins International Airport (CLE) is southwest of downtown and directly connected by the Red Line, which is handy for renters without a car.</p>',
    'tips' => [
      'interns'  => 'Downtown and Ohio City are convenient for office internships, with the Red Line and buses linking them to the rest of the city. Summer is the best season to enjoy the lakefront and neighborhood festivals.',
      'nurses'   => 'The Cleveland Clinic main campus, University Hospitals Cleveland Medical Center, MetroHealth and the Louis Stokes Cleveland VA Medical Center are major employers. The HealthLine on Euclid Avenue makes University Circle, Little Italy and Cleveland Heights practical bases for both the Clinic and UH.',
      'students' => 'Case Western Reserve University is in University Circle, Cleveland State University is downtown and John Carroll University is in University Heights. Housing near Case turns over at the end of the spring semester.',
      'seasonal' => 'Summer is the most popular season for short stays, while winter can bring better availability in exchange for snow and cold. Medical housing demand is steady year-round.',
    ],
    'faqs' => [
      ['q' => 'Where should I stay near the Cleveland Clinic?', 'a' => 'University Circle, Little Italy, Cleveland Heights and parts of Midtown are close, and the HealthLine bus runs right past the main campus along Euclid Avenue.'],
      ['q' => 'Can I get from the airport to the city without a car?', 'a' => 'Yes. The RTA Red Line runs from Cleveland Hopkins directly to downtown and University Circle.'],
      ['q' => 'What should I know about winter rentals?', 'a' => 'Ask about off-street parking, snow removal and how heat is billed, since older homes can be costly to heat.'],
    ],
  ],

  'ca/san-jose' => [
