      ['name' => 'Japantown', 'blurb' => 'One of the few remaining historic Japantowns in the US, just north of downtown with older homes and apartments.'],
      ['name' => 'Rose Garden', 'blurb' => 'A leafy neighborhood west of downtown with classic homes, close to Santa Clara and Diridon Station.'],
      ['name' => 'North San Jose', 'blurb' => 'A large cluster of newer apartment complexes near tech offices and VTA light rail. Practical for interns and new hires.'],
      ['name' => 'West San Jose', 'blurb' => 'Near Santana Row and Valley Fair shopping, with access to Cupertino and Santa Clara offices.'],
      ['name' => 'Berryessa', 'blurb' => 'A northeast area with a BART station connecting to the East Bay, convenient for renters commuting north.'],
    ],
    'prices' => '<p>San Jose is expensive. Furnished private rooms commonly advertise somewhere in the $1,200&ndash;$2,000 per month range, and entire furnished one-bedrooms are usually considerably higher, often $2,500 or more, with newer buildings near tech campuses at the top.</p><p>Summer intern season can push prices up. Numbers swing with intern season, neighborhood and furnishing, so compare current listings and confirm what utilities and parking are included.</p>',
    'transit'=> '<p>VTA runs light rail and buses across Santa Clara County. Caltrain runs from San Jose Diridon north along the Peninsula to San Francisco, and BART reaches the Milpitas and Berryessa/North San Jos&eacute; stations. Even so, many residents drive.</p><p>San Jos&eacute; Mineta International Airport (SJC) is just north of downtown, and San Francisco International (SFO) is also within reach.</p>',
    'tips' => [
      'interns'  => 'Look for housing near your employer&rsquo;s campus or on a direct VTA or Caltrain line, since highway traffic can be heavy. Many interns share rooms or homes to manage costs, and summer listings fill early in spring.',
      'nurses'   => 'Major hospitals include Santa Clara Valley Medical Center, Regional Medical Center, O&rsquo;Connor Hospital, Good Samaritan Hospital and Kaiser Permanente facilities in San Jose and Santa Clara. Stanford Health Care in Palo Alto is also within driving distance.',
      'students' => 'San Jos&eacute; State University is downtown, Santa Clara University is in neighboring Santa Clara and Stanford University is in Palo Alto. Rooms near SJSU often become available for summer.',
      'seasonal' => 'Demand peaks in late spring and summer with intern arrivals. The academic calendar at SJSU and Santa Clara also drives turnover in May and August.',
