    'transit'=> '<p>RIPTA runs buses across Providence and the rest of Rhode Island. Providence Station is served by Amtrak and by the MBTA Providence/Stoughton commuter rail line to Boston. The city is walkable, but steep hills on the East Side are worth keeping in mind.</p><p>Rhode Island T.F. Green International Airport (PVD) is in Warwick, south of the city, and is connected by commuter rail as well as by car.</p>',
