    'intro'  => '<p>Milwaukee is a lakefront city with strong neighborhood identities and a manageable cost of living. Universities, a large medical complex in Wauwatosa, manufacturing and corporate headquarters bring interns, travel nurses, medical students and project workers who need furnished housing for a few months.</p><p>The <strong>Historic Third Ward</strong> is a former warehouse district now full of lofts, boutiques and restaurants, the <strong>East Side</strong> stretches along the lake near UW&ndash;Milwaukee, and <strong>Bay View</strong> to the south has a laid-back, neighborhood-bar feel. West of the city, Wauwatosa is home to the Milwaukee Regional Medical Center.</p><p>Winters are cold and snowy, but summers are lively with festivals and lakefront activities. Ask about heating, parking and winter street rules if you rent during the colder months. Lakefront parks and the downtown Riverwalk make summer stays especially appealing, and the city is close enough to Chicago for easy weekend trips.</p>',
