    ],
    'prices' => '<p>Milwaukee is affordable compared with many lakefront cities. Furnished private rooms commonly advertise somewhere in the $550&ndash;$950 per month range, and entire furnished one-bedrooms typically run higher, often $1,100&ndash;$1,800 depending on the neighborhood.</p><p>The Third Ward and lakefront buildings tend to be priciest. Summer festival season, location and furnishings all influence rates, so browse current listings to see where the market sits.</p>',
    'transit'=> '<p>The Milwaukee County Transit System (MCTS) runs buses, including the CONNECT 1 bus rapid transit line linking downtown with Wauwatosa and the medical center. The Hop streetcar serves downtown and the Third Ward. Amtrak&rsquo;s Hiawatha service runs to Chicago from downtown and the airport station.</p><p>Milwaukee Mitchell International Airport (MKE) is south of downtown, about 15 minutes by car.</p>',
    'tips' => [
      'interns'  => 'The Third Ward and downtown are convenient for corporate internships, with The Hop and bus service nearby. Summer festivals make it a fun season to be in the city.',
      'nurses'   => 'Froedtert Hospital and Children&rsquo;s Wisconsin are at the Milwaukee Regional Medical Center in Wauwatosa, and Aurora St. Luke&rsquo;s Medical Center, Ascension Columbia St. Mary&rsquo;s and the Zablocki VA Medical Center are also major employers. Wauwatosa and the CONNECT 1 corridor work well for the regional medical center.',
      'students' => 'UW&ndash;Milwaukee, Marquette University, the Milwaukee School of Engineering and the Medical College of Wisconsin are the main institutions. The East Side and areas near Marquette are popular student neighborhoods.',
      'seasonal' => 'Summer is peak season, with Summerfest in late June and early July and other lakefront festivals filling the calendar. Late summer is busy as students return.',
    ],
    'faqs' => [
      ['q' => 'Where should I stay near Froedtert or Children&rsquo;s Wisconsin?', 'a' => 'Wauwatosa and nearby west-side neighborhoods are closest, and the CONNECT 1 bus links the medical center with downtown.'],
      ['q' => 'Can I get to Chicago easily?', 'a' => 'Yes. Amtrak&rsquo;s Hiawatha runs several times a day between Milwaukee and Chicago.'],
      ['q' => 'What should I know about winter rentals?', 'a' => 'Ask about heating costs, off-street parking and snow removal, since winters are long.'],
    ],
