    'tagline'=> 'Furnished short-term rentals in North Carolina&rsquo;s capital and the Research Triangle, from Glenwood South to North Hills.',
    'intro'  => '<p>Raleigh anchors the Research Triangle along with Durham and Chapel Hill, and the region&rsquo;s universities, state government, hospitals and the Research Triangle Park business district create steady demand for furnished, flexible housing. Interns, legislative staff, travel nurses, researchers and relocating professionals are all part of the market.</p><p>Downtown districts like <strong>Glenwood South</strong> and the <strong>Warehouse District</strong> offer apartments near restaurants and nightlife, while historic neighborhoods such as <strong>Oakwood</strong> and <strong>Five Points</strong> have older homes on tree-lined streets. <strong>North Hills</strong> is a newer, mixed-use area in Midtown Raleigh, and the area around NC State and Hillsborough Street is popular with students.</p><p>The Triangle is spread out, and many renters commute between Raleigh, Durham, RTP and Cary, so check the route to your office before you choose. An extensive greenway network runs through much of the city, a plus for renters who like to walk, run or bike.</p>',
    'neighborhoods' => [
      ['name' => 'Glenwood South', 'blurb' => 'A lively downtown district with apartments, bars and restaurants. Popular with young professionals.'],
      ['name' => 'Warehouse District', 'blurb' => 'Converted industrial buildings and newer apartments on the west side of downtown.'],
      ['name' => 'Oakwood', 'blurb' => 'A historic neighborhood of Victorian homes just east of downtown.'],
      ['name' => 'Five Points', 'blurb' => 'An established residential area north of downtown with local shops and restaurants.'],
      ['name' => 'North Hills', 'blurb' => 'A walkable mixed-use center in Midtown with newer apartments and shopping, close to the Beltline.'],
      ['name' => 'Hillsborough Street and NC State area', 'blurb' => 'Student-oriented housing near NC State University, with many summer sublets.'],
      ['name' => 'Cameron Village area', 'blurb' => 'A shopping district between downtown and NC State with apartments nearby.'],
    ],
    'prices' => '<p>Raleigh has become pricier as the region has grown. Furnished private rooms commonly advertise somewhere around $700&ndash;$1,100 per month, and entire furnished one-bedrooms typically run higher, often $1,400&ndash;$2,200 depending on the area.</p><p>Downtown and North Hills tend to cost more. Use these numbers only as a rough guide; season, neighborhood and furnishing change them, so compare current listings.</p>',
    'transit'=> '<p>GoRaleigh runs city buses and GoTriangle provides regional buses to Durham, Chapel Hill and RTP. Most residents drive, and the I-40 and I-440 corridors can be congested at rush hour.</p><p>Raleigh-Durham International Airport (RDU) sits between Raleigh and Durham, about 20 to 25 minutes from downtown Raleigh by car.</p>',
    'tips' => [
      'interns'  => 'If your internship is in RTP, consider living in west Raleigh or nearby areas to shorten the commute. Downtown internships, including state government positions near the Capitol, pair well with Glenwood South or Oakwood.',
      'nurses'   => 'WakeMed, UNC Rex Hospital and Duke Raleigh Hospital are major employers in Raleigh, and Duke University Hospital in Durham and UNC Medical Center in Chapel Hill are within driving distance. North Hills and areas near Wade Avenue are convenient for several Raleigh hospitals.',
      'students' => 'NC State University is the largest school in Raleigh, along with Meredith College, Shaw University and William Peace University. Duke University and UNC&ndash;Chapel Hill are nearby in the Triangle.',
      'seasonal' => 'Summer brings interns and some student sublets, while August is busy as students return. Legislative sessions can also increase demand for downtown short stays.',
    ],
    'faqs' => [
