    'intro'  => '<p>Oklahoma City is a sprawling, affordable metro with a growing downtown core. The energy industry, state government, Tinker Air Force Base and the city&rsquo;s large medical centers bring travel nurses, contractors, military personnel and relocating professionals who need furnished housing on flexible terms.</p><p>The central city has seen a lot of investment. <strong>Midtown</strong> and <strong>Automobile Alley</strong> offer apartments in restored buildings near downtown, <strong>Bricktown</strong> is an entertainment district along a canal, and the <strong>Plaza District</strong> and Paseo Arts District have a creative, local character. Historic residential neighborhoods like Mesta Park and Heritage Hills are close to downtown.</p><p>OKC is very car-oriented, and spring is severe weather season, so ask about shelter options and parking when choosing a rental. Scissortail Park and the Oklahoma River have added parks and recreation close to downtown in recent years. Rents are low enough that many mid-term renters can afford an entire furnished apartment rather than a room, which is not true in many larger metros.</p>',
