      ['name' => 'Bricktown', 'blurb' => 'An entertainment district with a canal, ballpark and apartments, popular for short stays.'],
      ['name' => 'Automobile Alley', 'blurb' => 'Former car dealerships converted into lofts and restaurants along Broadway.'],
      ['name' => 'Plaza District', 'blurb' => 'An artsy neighborhood west of downtown with shops, murals and older homes.'],
      ['name' => 'Paseo Arts District', 'blurb' => 'A small district of galleries and Spanish-style buildings.'],
      ['name' => 'Mesta Park and Heritage Hills', 'blurb' => 'Historic neighborhoods with large older homes close to downtown and Midtown.'],
      ['name' => 'Nichols Hills', 'blurb' => 'An upscale enclave north of the city with quiet streets and nearby shopping.'],
    ],
    'prices' => '<p>Oklahoma City is among the more affordable large metros. Furnished private rooms commonly advertise somewhere around $500&ndash;$850 per month, and entire furnished one-bedrooms typically run higher, often $950&ndash;$1,600 depending on location.</p><p>Newer downtown and Midtown buildings sit at the higher end. Actual prices depend on season, neighborhood and furnishing, so check current listings for up-to-date figures.</p>',
    'transit'=> '<p>EMBARK runs city buses, the OKC Streetcar downtown and RAPID bus service on the northwest side. Most residents drive, and the city is designed around highways.</p><p>Will Rogers International Airport (OKC) is southwest of downtown, around 15 to 20 minutes by car.</p>',
    'tips' => [
      'interns'  => 'Downtown, Midtown and Automobile Alley are convenient for office internships and offer some walkability. A car is still very useful for errands and weekend trips.',
      'nurses'   => 'OU Health University of Oklahoma Medical Center, INTEGRIS Health Baptist Medical Center, Mercy Hospital Oklahoma City and SSM Health St. Anthony Hospital are major employers. Midtown and the areas north of downtown are central to several of them.',
      'students' => 'The University of Oklahoma Health Sciences Center is in OKC, Oklahoma City University is near the Plaza District and the University of Central Oklahoma is in Edmond. The main OU campus is in Norman to the south.',
