    'prices' => '<p>Furnished private rooms in New Orleans commonly advertise somewhere around $700&ndash;$1,200 per month, and entire furnished one-bedrooms typically run higher, often $1,400&ndash;$2,400 depending on neighborhood.</p><p>Prices can spike around Mardi Gras and Jazz Fest. Festival season, neighborhood and furnishing make a big difference here, so compare current listings for your exact dates.</p>',
    'transit'=> '<p>The New Orleans Regional Transit Authority (RTA) runs the city&rsquo;s famous streetcars, including the St. Charles, Canal and Rampart lines, plus buses and the Algiers ferry. Many residents still drive, but central neighborhoods are bikeable and walkable.</p><p>Louis Armstrong New Orleans International Airport (MSY) is in Kenner, about 25 minutes west of downtown by car.</p>',
    'tips' => [
      'interns'  => 'The CBD and Lower Garden District are convenient for downtown internships. Summer is hot and humid, so check that air conditioning works well.',
      'nurses'   => 'Ochsner Medical Center, University Medical Center New Orleans, Tulane Medical Center, Children&rsquo;s Hospital New Orleans, Touro Infirmary and the Southeast Louisiana Veterans Health Care System are major employers. The CBD and Mid-City are close to the downtown medical district.',
      'students' => 'Tulane University, Loyola University New Orleans, the University of New Orleans, Xavier University of Louisiana, Dillard University and LSU Health New Orleans are all here. Uptown is popular with Tulane and Loyola students.',
      'seasonal' => 'Mardi Gras in late winter and Jazz Fest in late April and early May are the biggest peaks. Summer is slower, and hurricane season runs June through November.',
    ],
    'faqs' => [
      ['q' => 'Are monthly rentals allowed in New Orleans?', 'a' => 'The city regulates short-term rentals closely. Confirm with the host that the stay is set up as a monthly rental and get a written agreement.'],
      ['q' => 'When is the hardest time to find a rental?', 'a' => 'Around Mardi Gras and Jazz Fest, when demand and prices spike.'],
      ['q' => 'Can I get around without a car?', 'a' => 'In Uptown, the Garden District, the CBD and Mid-City, the streetcars, bikes and walking cover a lot. A car helps for trips further out.'],
    ],
  ],

