      ['name' => 'Slatterly Park', 'blurb' => 'A residential area east of downtown with a mix of homes and apartments.'],
      ['name' => 'Saint Marys area', 'blurb' => 'Neighborhoods around Mayo Clinic Hospital, Saint Marys Campus, southwest of downtown.'],
      ['name' => 'Northwest Rochester', 'blurb' => 'Newer apartment complexes and homes, practical for renters with cars.'],
    ],
    'prices' => '<p>Furnished private rooms in Rochester commonly advertise somewhere around $600&ndash;$1,000 per month, and entire furnished one-bedrooms typically run higher, often $1,200&ndash;$1,900 depending on location and proximity to Mayo.</p><p>Places connected to the skyway or within walking distance of Mayo tend to cost more. Season, distance to Mayo and furnishing level all move prices, so compare current listings for your dates.</p>',
    'transit'=> '<p>Rochester Public Transit (RPT) runs city buses, and downtown is connected by an extensive skyway and pedestrian subway system linking Mayo Clinic buildings, hotels and shops. Many renters drive, especially outside downtown.</p><p>Rochester International Airport (RST) has limited service, and many travelers fly into Minneapolis&ndash;Saint Paul International Airport (MSP), roughly a 90 minute drive north; shuttle services run between MSP and Rochester.</p>',
    'tips' => [
